# ============================================================================
# EmailJS (optional) — contact form email delivery
# ============================================================================
# The contact form works out of the box in a client-side DEMO mode (no backend
# required): a valid submit is acknowledged honestly as a local demo and NO
# email is sent. To enable REAL email delivery via EmailJS, copy this file to a
# local, git-ignored env file and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the client bundle by Vite
# (read as import.meta.env.VITE_*).
#
# ACTIVATION CONTRACT (src/hooks/useContactForm.js):
#   Real delivery is attempted ONLY when VITE_EMAILJS_ENABLED is exactly "true"
#   AND all three credentials below are set AND the EmailJS SDK has been wired
#   in (see the post-merge steps). This means:
#     * Leaving VITE_EMAILJS_ENABLED unset (or not "true") keeps the form in the
#       safe demo mode even if you fill in the three credentials — so setting the
#       keys ALONE never switches on delivery and never breaks the form.
#     * Setting VITE_EMAILJS_ENABLED="true" WITHOUT all three credentials (or
#       before wiring in the SDK) surfaces a controlled "couldn't send" error
#       rather than pretending to send.
#
# Where to find these values (EmailJS dashboard — https://www.emailjs.com/):
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID   -> Email Services
#   VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID  -> Email Templates
#   VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY   -> Account > API Keys (publishable public key)
#
# SECURITY: put REAL values only in .env.local (ignored via the *.local rule
# in .gitignore) — never commit them. The public key is browser-publishable;
# do NOT place any private/secret keys in the client env.
#
# Post-merge prerequisites for real delivery (see README "Post-Merge Manual
# Steps"): (1) npm install @emailjs/browser; (2) convert the deferred
# @vite-ignore dynamic import in useContactForm.js into a statically analyzable
# import so Vite bundles the SDK; (3) set the flag + credentials and rebuild.
# ============================================================================

# Master opt-in switch for real EmailJS delivery. Must be exactly "true" to
# activate; any other value (including unset) keeps the safe demo mode.
VITE_EMAILJS_ENABLED=

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
